/T (Reason:  1\) By implementing a rule that requires the bar to be positioned above the shoulder blades, ensures it is not set too low on the back and assists in preventing excessive forward bending at the start of the lift.  In addition, this measure is intended to protect Sub-Junior and Junior lifters from increased risk of lower back injuries and excessive loading on the lumbar \(lower\) spine, as these athletes may not yet be fully developed physically, muscularly, or technically. )
